  "prompt": "You are an expert JavaScript developer. Create a single-page, standalone HTML document containing a fully playable \"Tango\" logic puzzle game.\n\nSTRICT TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n1. ALL HTML, CSS, and JavaScript must be contained within a single file. No external libraries.\n2. Do NOT output markdown code blocks (```html). Start exactly with <!DOCTYPE html> and end with </html>.\n\nTHEME & VISUALS:\n1. The game must look polished and modern, utilizing a clean, balanced interface.\n2. The grid must be 6x6 cells.\n3. The two playing symbols MUST be the Fire emoji (\ud83d\udd25) and the Ice Cube emoji (\ud83e\uddca).\n4. Constraint markers must clearly sit on the borders between adjacent cells using an Equals sign (=) or a Cross (\u00d7).\n\nCORE GAMEPLAY RULES:\n1. Row and Column Balance: Every row and every column must contain exactly three \ud83d\udd25 and three \ud83e\uddca.\n2. No Three in a Row: You cannot place three identical symbols adjacent to each other horizontally or vertically.\n3. Constraint Markers:\n   - '=' (Equals): The two adjacent cells must contain the same symbol.\n   - '\u00d7' (Cross): The two adjacent cells must contain opposite symbols.\n4. Interactivity: Clicking a cell should cycle its state: Empty -> \ud83d\udd25 -> \ud83e\uddca -> Empty.\n\nBACK-END LOGIC & PROCEDURAL GENERATION SPECS:\nThe game MUST generate a brand new, random, playable board on every page load. Implement the generation using this sequence:\n1. Solution Generation (Backtracking): Write a recursive backtracking function to generate a fully populated, valid 6x6 grid that obeys the Balance and No-Three-In-A-Row rules. \n2. Constraint Placement: Once a valid solved board exists, randomly select 6 to 8 pairs of adjacent cells. If the cells share the same symbol, place an '=' marker between them. If they are different, place an '\u00d7' marker.\n3. Puzzle Creation: After placing constraints, randomly clear (empty) 70% of the cells, leaving a few starting symbols and the constraint markers as hints for the player.\n4. Validation: Implement a \"Check Solution\" button that compares the user's current grid against the underlying rules (Balance, No-Three-In-A-Row, and Constraints). Highlight any errors in red.\n\nEnsure the state management clearly separates the \"solution board\" from the \"player board\", and that markers overlay the grid lines cleanly using CSS absolute positioning or a highly refined Grid layout.\n",
  "rawOutput": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<title>Tango Puzzle</title>\n<style>\n  body { margin:0; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; background:#f0f4f8; }\n  #game { display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center; }\n  .grid, .markers { position:relative; width:100%; height:100%; }\n  .cell { width:100px; height:100px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; border:1px solid #ccc; }\n  .empty { background:#fff; }\n  .symbol { font-size:1.5rem; }\n  .error { background:#ffcccc; }\n  #checkBtn { margin-top:10px; padding:5px 10px; cursor:pointer; }\n  button { background:#007bff; color:#fff; border:none; padding:5px 10px; border-radius:4px; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"game\">\n  <div id=\"checkBtn\" onclick=\"checkSolution()\">Check Solution</button>\n</div>\n<div class=\"grid\" id=\"grid\"></div>\n<div class=\"markers\" id=\"markers\"></div>\n\n<script>\nconst ROWS = 6, COLS = 6, CELL_SIZE = 100;\nconst symbols = [1,2]; // 1 heat, 2 ice\n\nlet board = Array.from({length: ROWS}, () => Array(COLS).fill(0));\n\nfunction canPlace(r, c, sym) {\n    // row count\n    let rowCnt = board[r].filter(x => x === sym).length;\n    if (rowCnt === 3) return false;\n    // column count\n    let colCnt = board.slice(r).filter(row => row[c] === sym).length;\n    if (colCnt === 3) return false;\n    // three in a row horizontally\n    let leftCnt = 0;\n    for (let i = c-2; i >= 0; i--) {\n        if (board[r][i] === sym) leftCnt++;\n        else break;\n    }\n    if (leftCnt === 2) return false;\n    // three in a row vertically\n    let topCnt = 0;\n    for (let i = r-2; i >= 0; i--) {\n        if (board[i][c] === sym) topCnt++;\n        else break;\n    }\n    if (topCnt === 2) return false;\n    return true;\n}\n\nfunction dfs(r, c) {\n    if (r === ROWS) return true;\n    let nc = c + 1;\n    if (nc >= COLS) {\n        r++;\n        nc = 0;\n    }\n    // try heat\n    if (canPlace(r, c, 1) && board[r][c] === 0) {\n        board[r][c] = 1;\n        if (dfs(r, nc)) return true;\n        board[r][c] = 0;\n    }\n    // try ice\n    if (canPlace(r, c, 2) && board[r][c] === 0) {\n        board[r][c] = 2;\n        if (dfs(r, nc)) return true;\n        board[r][c] = 0;\n    }\n    return false;\n}\n\nfunction initSolution() {\n    dfs(0, 0);\n}\n\n// generate solution board\ninitSolution();\n\n// place constraints\nconst allAdjs = [];\nfor (let r = 0; r < ROWS; r++) {\n    for (let c = 0; c < COLS; c++) {\n        if (c + 1 < COLS) allAdjs.push({r, c, 'right'});\n    }\n    if (r + 1 < ROWS) allAdjs.push({r, c, 'down'});\n}\nconst constraints = [];\nlet rnd = Math.random;\nfunction pick() {\n    if (constraints.length < 6 || constraints.length > 8) return false;\n    return rnd() < 0.2;\n}\nwhile (constraints.length < 6) {\n    if (pick()) constraints.push({r: Math.floor(rnd()*ROWS), c: Math.floor(rnd()*COLS, 2), dir: rnd() ? 'right' : 'down'});\n}\n\nfunction placeConstraints() {\n    const overlay = document.getElementById('markers');\n    overlay.innerHTML = '';\n    for (const adj of constraints) {\n        const {r, c, dir} = adj;\n        const symbol = board[r][c] === 1 ? '\ud83d\udd25' : board[r][c] === 2 ? '\ud83e\uddca' : '';\n        const marker = document.createElement('span');\n        marker.className = 'marker';\n        marker.textContent = symbol;\n        const left = c * CELL_SIZE + CELL_SIZE/2 + CELL_SIZE/2 - (symbol.length*8);\n        const top = r * CELL_SIZE + CELL_SIZE/2;\n        overlay.appendChild(marker);\n    }\n}\n\n// clear cells\nfunction clearCells() {\n    const total = ROWS * COLS;\n    const cellsToClear = Math.ceil(total * 0.7);\n    const cleared = new Set();\n    while (cleared.size < cellsToClear) {\n        let r = rnd() % ROWS;\n        let c = rnd() % COLS;\n        cleared.add(r * COLS + c);\n    }\n    for (let i = 0; i < total; i++) {\n        if (!cleared.has(i)) {\n            board[i / COLS][i % COLS] = 0;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfunction renderBoard() {\n    const grid = document.getElementById('grid');\n    grid.innerHTML = '';\n    for (let r = 0; r < ROWS; r++) {\n        for (let c = 0; c < COLS; c++) {\n            const cell = board[r][c];\n            const cellEl = document.createElement('div');\n            cellEl.className = 'cell';\n            if (cell !== 0) {\n                cellEl.textContent = symbols[cell];\n                cellEl.classList.add('symbol');\n            }\n            grid.appendChild(cellEl);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfunction validateBoard() {\n    const errors = [];\n    // row/col balance\n    for (let r = 0; r < ROWS; r++) {\n        let heat = 0, ice = 0;\n        for (let c = 0; c < COLS; c++) {\n            if (board[r][c] === 1) heat++;\n            else if (board[r][c] === 2) ice++;\n        }\n        if (heat !== 3 || ice !== 3) errors.push(`Row ${r+1}`);\n    }\n    for (let c = 0; c < COLS; c++) {\n        let heat = 0, ice = 0;\n        for (let r = 0; r < ROWS; r++) {\n            if (board[r][c] === 1) heat++;\n            else if (board[r][c] === 2) ice++;\n        }\n        if (heat !== 3 || ice !== 3) errors.push(`Column ${c+1}`);\n    }\n    // three in a row\n    for (let r = 0; r < ROWS; r++) {\n        for (let c = 0; c < COLS - 2; c++) {\n            let same = 0;\n            for (let k = 0; k < 3; k++) {\n                if (board[r][c+k] === 1) same++;\n                else if (board[r][c+k] === 2) same++;\n            }\n            if (same >= 3) errors.push(`Row ${r+1} col ${c+1}`);\n        }\n        for (let k = 0; k < ROWS - 2; k++) {\n            let same = 0;\n            for (let l = 0; l < 3; l++) {\n                if (board[r+l][c] === 1) same++;\n                else if (board[r+l][c] === 2) same++;\n            }\n            if (same >= 3) errors.push(`Column ${c+1} row ${r+1}`);\n        }\n    }\n    // constraint markers\n    for (const adj of constraints) {\n        const {r, c, dir} = adj;\n        const left = c * CELL_SIZE + CELL_SIZE/2 + CELL_SIZE/2 - (symbols[board[r][c]]?.length*8);\n        const top = r * CELL_SIZE + CELL_SIZE/2;\n        const marker = document.querySelector(`.marker:nth-of-type(${adj.r*COLS + adj.c})`);\n        if (marker) {\n            if ((board[r][c] === 1 && board[r][c+1] === 1) || (board[r][c] === 2 && board[r][c+1] === 2)) {\n                marker.classList.add('error');\n            } else if ((board[r][c] !== 1 && board[r][c+1] !== 1)) {\n                marker.classList.add('error');\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return errors;\n}\n\nfunction checkSolution() {\n    const errs = validateBoard();\n    if (errs.length) {\n        errs.forEach(e => {\n            const el = document.querySelector(`.error:nth-of-type(${errs.length})`);\n            if (!el) el = document.createElement('span');\n            el.className = 'error';\n            el.textContent = e;\n            document.body.appendChild(el);\n        });\n    } else {\n        document.body.innerHTML = `<p style=\"color:green;\">All checks passed!</p>`;\n    }\n}\n\ndocument.getElementById('checkBtn').addEventListener('click', checkSolution);\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>",
